cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Echo AI Analysis: an end-to-end pipeline for echocardiographic segmentation, motion tracking and ejection fraction estimation"
message: "If you use this software or its findings in your work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rangraz
    given-names: Parisa
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/ParisaRangraz/echo-ai-analysis"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end pipeline for echocardiographic image analysis on the public
  CAMUS dataset: speckle denoising, multi-structure segmentation of the apical
  two- and four-chamber views, deformable registration to propagate the
  end-diastolic mask through the cardiac cycle, biplane Simpson volume
  estimation, and classification of left ventricular ejection fraction.
  Three segmentation architectures are compared end to end, including a
  reverse-attention decoder on a PVTv2 encoder.
keywords:
  - echocardiography
  - medical image segmentation
  - image registration
  - ejection fraction
  - ultrasound
  - CAMUS
license: MIT
